# CareerGem Agentic Build Mandate

## Product Vision

CareerGem turns job seeking into a math problem.

Input: resume + target roles.

Output: readiness assessment + 3-5 concrete actions.

Tone: advisor who runs numbers, not cheerleader.

## Immediate Build: Phase 1-3 (Onboarding, Assessment, Guidance)

See the system prompt titled "CareerGem Lovable Pro Prompt" for full specs.

## Non-Negotiable Constraints

- All assessment model calls happen server-side only. In this codebase that means
  TanStack Start server functions (`createServerFn`) with `*.server.ts` helpers —
  never client-side, never a raw client key. (Original mandate said "Supabase Edge
  Functions"; this stack uses server functions instead.)

- Zero resume text or parsed data exposed to client unencrypted.

- Preserve existing Supabase auth, RLS, and entitlement checks.

- Payment status is single source of truth for free/Pro gates.

- No "AI" language in UI ("Assessment" not "AI Assessment").

- Shareable snippet export is mandatory (content flywheel input).

## Code Quality Gates

- Every new page has a test.

- No env secrets in client code.

- TypeScript strict mode.

- All forms have validation + error states.

- RLS policies audited before deploy.

## Deployment Contract

- Before deploy: run tests, lint, type check.

- After deploy: spot-check the /onboarding flow, trigger a test assessment.

- Flag anything requiring manual verification (API costs, content accuracy).

## Do Not Build Without Explicit Instruction

- Messaging/networking.

- Job board scraping.

- Certification tracking.

- Interview prep (video/practice).

Build only what's in the CareerGem prompt. Ask for clarification if ambiguous.